{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities","id":1555342,"title":"Your favorite and least favorite V:TM cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-11-10T17:55:53-08:00","id":1555342,"title":"Your favorite and least favorite V:TM cities","content":"Basically, what the title says.<br /> <br /> The city sourcebooks were something of a poisoned chalice in terms of V:TM's development. Chicago by Night helped illustrate how the game world functioned and gave a huge boost to shared terminology, titles, and archetypes (Lodin seems like he's the basis for a lot of Ventrue princes, IMHO)<br /> <br /> However, the game books have always had a limited appeal because unless you planned to do your game in one of those cities, there wasn't much appeal to it. After all, if you didn't intend to run a game in New Orleans then you probably don't need the sourcebook. It's probably too much for a night trip too.<br /> <br /> The sourcebooks are obvious but feel free to also include the cities described in things like Let the Streets Run Red like Indianapolis.<br /> <br /> <b>Favorite</b><br /> <br /> <i>Gary Indiana</i><br /> <br /> Yeah, no surprise here and I should probably include it as part of the greater Chicago Chronicles but I think it was a fantastic introduction to how V:TM works. The game isn't about fighting an<br /> enemy. The game is about...talking. It's the Seinfeld effect except instead of a diner, you just go to the Succubus Club.<br /> <br /> Here, Modius has enslaved the beautiful Allicia and is an insane Ms. Havisham-esque fop of a prince.<br /> <br /> Juggler claims to be the heroic champion of the Anarchs and Neonates but he also has enslaved the beautiful Evelyn in the same way.<br /> <br /> There's hunters after the PCs but killing them would make it worse and the best thing to do is to figure out something nonviolent to do it.<br /> <br /> Lucian is a 2000 year old Methusaleh who is 8th generation and thus not a Jhyad major player. There's also a Nosferatu seeking Golconda.<br /> <br /> Michael? He's <i>Of Mice and Men</i> in the making, isn't he?<br /> <br /> <b>Least</b><br /> <br /> <i>Los Angeles by Night</i><br /> <br /> This may surprise some people as this since most people agree this is the 2nd best sourcebook and it certainly led to a lot of awesome stuff like Bloodlines and LA by Night. However, I think that was because of what was built on Los Angeles by Night and retconned a lot of it.<br /> <br /> However, I think Los Angeles by Night seriously hurt the Anarch movement for the future of the line.<br /> <br /> Basically, so much of the Anarchs are defined by LA Gang culture, feuding over turf, and just being Brujah as well as Caiitiff with rare exceptions. I feel like compared to Maldavis, they really don't have anyone inspiring to join the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it has Bela and Bela is awesome.\u200b<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T21:46:56-08:00","id":1555347,"title":"","content":"I'm not a fan of city books, but I have to agree about LA.<br /> <br /> One overall problem I have is that the city books ended up calcifying a lot of stereotypes instead of exploring possibilities. A lot of what both fans and writers expect about how Kindred will be and organize is just copying the early city books to some extent instead of diverging from them.<br /> <br /> LA defined and destroyed the Anarchs in this process. No one ever dared to build alternatives and so their bland brand of &quot;anarchy&quot; became what the movement is in the game. It sucks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T22:08:29-08:00","id":1555348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555347#post1555347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a fan of city books, but I have to agree about LA.<br /> <br /> One overall problem I have is that the city books ended up calcifying a lot of stereotypes instead of exploring possibilities. A lot of what both fans and writers expect about how Kindred will be and organize is just copying the early city books to some extent instead of diverging from them.<br /> <br /> LA defined and destroyed the Anarchs in this process. No one ever dared to build alternatives and so their bland brand of &quot;anarchy&quot; became what the movement is in the game. It sucks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Chicago by Night had a much better and still chaotic idea of what the Anarchs represented:<br /> <br /> * You have Tyler as the original Brujah sellout, someone who killed an ancient Ventrue (that became way more important overall) and helped found the Anarchs as we know them but now is just comfortable being a richer than God Kindred on the Primogen.<br /> * You had the Trotsky-esque socialists with Blackjack, Modius (who was an Anarch sellout), and characters from The Jungle.<br /> * You had the 1970s Black Panther movement that had become angry and violent BECAUSE of the way they'd been treated as angry and violent.<br /> * You had Maldavis representing the next generation of Civil Rights leadership stabbed in the back by their Primogen sponsors. People who sought to reform the system only to find out that the system had no interest in reform.<br /> * You had Juggler representing controlled opposition with him working for Tyler, the original Brujah sellout. Also, people like Uriah, Gordon Keaton, and Gengis who are Anarchs in name only.<br /> <br /> They didn't get along but they all had ideas of how to reform Kindred society and an intellectual side (except for Gengis).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T22:22:02-08:00","id":1555350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555348#post1555348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Chicago by Night had a much better and still chaotic idea of what the Anarchs represented:</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably, but as a Camarilla city it meant little for many people. LA got to be the face of the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Instead Chicago was one of the sources on how a Camarilla city works, and crystallized the overly formal structure of positions people now want to impose upon cities with a fraction of its size.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines</i> also had a better idea for the Camarilla: you need a Prince and a Sheriff, anything else is just political opportunism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-10T23:32:47-08:00","id":1555351,"title":"","content":"Never been the big fan of City books, they a bit missed the target in my humble opinion...<br /> ..but if I have to choose? Then <i>Mexico City by Night</i> delivered and was quite good","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T09:19:55-08:00","id":1555360,"title":"","content":"As a Washingtonian by birth, have a special fondness some parts of DC by night. Peep my forum handle if you don't believe me.<br /> <br /> First, let me say that I don't think its unusual for a native of a region depicted in a &quot;By Night&quot; or &quot;Rage Across&quot; book to have, shall we say, <i>pointed</i> opinions on its portrayal. It doesn't seem there was any sort of requirement for the writer to have lived in the region for any length of time. And, to be fair, most of these were written before Wikipedia was a thing (or at least widely used). But I still feel like, despite some big hits, DC by Night had several problems.<br /> <br /> The Geography section reads like a tourist guide, with far too much attention on the various federal buildings but far too little attention to the neighborhoods where people actually live. The history section is phenomenal from the Colonial period up through the civil war. After that his interest in, ya know, the actual city of Washington DC seems to have waned. They misses out on a lot of the cities development as a center of (particularly African American) cultural expression and political struggle.<br /> <br /> I don't want to imply the author is, like committing a racism or something. But such disinterest in the cities actual residents has knock on effects elsewhere in the quality of the final product. Simply put, next time I wouldn't have someone from Mechanicsburg VA (300 miles away) write a book about Washington DC.<br /> <br /> In my opinion the fact it skips out on the cities diverse cultural history is made evident by the fact so few of the Vampires feel particularly tied to or part of the city. Most of them are broad enough vampiric stereotypes they could be slotted into almost any generic fictional ST created city. Ballet dancer Toreador. Serial Killer Malkavian. Drug runner Settite. Le yawn! Even Monica and Cynthia black are just kinda...there. No former intelligence agency Nossies? No Toreador with connection with any sort of black cultural product or era from the Chitlins Cricut through to Go-Go Music? No Brujah with any appreciable politics? In DC?!<br /> <br /> My dream book that never got published would be City of Magik by Night: Washington DC. Mage/Vamp crossover. My two favorite games? Set in my home town? Ancient vampires and technocratic masters playing 5th dimensional chess while walking on eggshells around mortal hunters? A vibrant sub-altern culture for Traditions mages and neonates of all sects to rub shoulders in? STICK IN IN MY VIENS!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6350-marcusvitel","name":"MarcusVitel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T15:41:22-08:00","id":1555376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarcusVitel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555360#post1555360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, let me say that I don't think its unusual for a native of a region depicted in a &quot;By Night&quot; or &quot;Rage Across&quot; book to have, shall we say, <i>pointed</i> opinions on its portrayal. It doesn't seem there was any sort of requirement for the writer to have lived in the region for any length of time. And, to be fair, most of these were written before Wikipedia was a thing (or at least widely used). But I still feel like, despite some big hits, DC by Night had several problems.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry for the bitterness, but that's just a small sample of what we felt the world over when our countries and cities were touched by White Wolf.<br /> <br /> I think while this is a valid complaint, it calls for a larger discussion than just the city books.<br /> <br /> None of them is a good depiction of their cities, except <b><i>maybe</i></b> if an author was a native, and I say maybe because they would still have a personal perspective. But that's that, given the time and all that you can't really expect much more (except you can, but that's whole another conversation).<br /> <br /> <i>Rage Across the Amazon</i> irks me to no end, and why the fuck did they put <i>Rio by Night</i> there!? It's like having <i>Houston by Night</i> in a book about the Great Lakes, except the distance is even greater!\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-11T16:09:05-08:00","id":1555377,"title":"","content":"Reviving my opinion, I think SAN FRANSISCO BY NIGHT is probably my least favorite of the WOD books as it infuriates me on virtually every level. I understand what the author was going for but I disagree that was a good idea in the first place and it manages to tick every one of those boxes that annoy me.<br /> <br /> Basically, the first issue is the lore ignorance. The author clearly wasn't familiar or interested in the Keith Herber San Fransisco created for the novels. That San Fransisco managed to incorporate the history of the Gold rush, gay rights movement, Spanish colonies, and the Chinese history of the city in a fascinating mixture of culture that Vannevar Thomas was the Prince of. All of that was discarded for the new Prince and characters because I'm fairly sure the authors didn't want to use any of that.<br /> <br /> That's not something I'm fond of as a lore junkie but then there's what San Fransisco by Night was about<b></b>: The Great Leap Outward and being a city where the Kindred are occupied. It more or less turns into a French Occupation story with the Kindred being oppressed victims of the Wan Kuei. Which is WEIRD and a bad allegory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T14:28:04-08:00","id":1555433,"title":"","content":"Chicago and Constantnople by Night were my favorite city books with the Fall of London &amp; Berlin by Night as my least favorite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-13T14:57:31-08:00","id":1555436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555433#post1555433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago and Constantnople by Night were my favorite city books with the Fall of London &amp; Berlin by Night as my least favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really? I thought The Fall of London was actually pretty good, not the least because it was much, much better than the Victorian Age Vampire version where they had Neonates as primogen.<br /> <br /> Berlin By Night I feel like would have been a fantastic supplement if they just removed the adventure and the Nazis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T07:03:26-08:00","id":1555756,"title":"","content":"City books are always useful, even if not for the city they're intended for, but I find nearly all of them have flaws. I would like to think we'd get better ones now, since Wikipedia and the internet make it easier to find local experts who can do a city well. <br /> <br /> <i>Fall of London</i> was terribad. <i>WoD: Hong Kong</i> is all kinds of goofy, offensive and OP, but at least is <i>fun</i>. I remember running a crossover game online for that, c. 2000, and I was inundated with requests to join. <i>LA by Night</i> has problems, but has a few good ideas and characters throughout.<br /> <br /> <i>Montreal by Night</i> is probably my favourite, minus some of the art choices and the trying-too-hard torture/snuff stuff. Yes, we get that it's a Sabbat city, but the edgelordiness is pretty cringe now. That said, the Irish Catholic in me obviously really digged all the dark mysticism of it.<br /> <br /> I think <i>Montreal by Night</i> is to the Sabbat what <i>Chicago by Night </i>was to the Camarilla, and the baroque decadence of the city just oozes ambience. <i>Mexico City by Night </i>has some cool stuff for showing the other parts of the Sabbat (especially its gratuitous violence), but felt like it was missing a little something.<br /> <br /> I've often wanted to write something about Manchester, where I live, as I've done a lot of research about the city over the years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T13:47:44-08:00","id":1555765,"title":"","content":"<b>Pro</b><br /> <br /> \u2022Chicago of course is the gold standard really. While I\u2019m someone who isn\u2019t a huge fan of all the 2nd edition killings, both are still all-timers in my opinion<br /> <br /> \u2022Washington D.C. by Night: I\u2019ll admit I have a couple biases here. My first ever VtM or WoD books were used copies of VtM 2e Core and Washington DC by Night from a local gaming shop &amp; I\u2019m a DelMarVa area native. That said, while I think it\u2019s got some really good gothic-punk imagery and vibes in it, if I\u2019m being totally honest with myself, Marcus Vitel does a lot of heavy lifting of actually making the book memorable or noteworthy. If it weren\u2019t for him becoming a popular and well known character this book probably would be read about as often as New Orleans or Milwaukee by Night. Still love it tho even though it\u2019s in desperate need of serious revisions and an actually good dramatic cast outside of the secret Lasombra and secret Sabbat characters<br /> <br /> <b>Anti</b><br /> <br /> To be clear, I don\u2019t so much hate these books as feel that they have a lot of missed potential<br /> <br /> \u2022New Orleans: there\u2019s some cool ideas in here but IMO it completely drops the ball on living up to how important and good a city like NO could have been for a setting like VtM that is so heavily indebted to Anne Rice. The Xaviar conclaves are cool and it\u2019s got some neat early cross-over stuff but it\u2019s largely forgettable. Really needs a stronger rewrite. I think the way that New Orleans got used for the VtR metaplot was really interesting and could be a possible reference point.<br /> <br /> \u2022L.A.: tbf I don\u2019t think it\u2019s that bad, but it\u2019s another case of missed opportunity IMO and it has to unlive with the reputation of having partly killed off interest in the Anarchs as a sect (not that Revised wouldn\u2019t help with that). I\u2019m not as against the gang elements as some people are, I think that any gothic-punk setting from the early-mid 90s would have had to be in dialogue with the massive cultural influence of those symbols in motifs in that era. But what L.A. needed to be was what Chicago by Night had been for the VtM Status Quo, LA had to be for the Anarchs. That\u2019s a tall order and it\u2019s not surprising that it came up short but it\u2019s still a mark on its record IMO. Plus the timeline gives me a headache when I try to square it with Demon, KotE, &amp; Bloodlines (which tbh I largely ignore in practice). Still some great work has been done on these very forums to flesh out the setting and that deserves a mention.<br /> <br /> \u2022NYC: this might be a hot take - I think the Tzimisce Antedeluviam being under NYC thing, while pretty funny and cool in theory, does more harm than good to the setting in theory long run. I admit this is totally subjective and that I would probably thing it was sick af in a particular chronicle (especially one with some Resident Evil type vibes) but IMO it feels a little too\u2026 I don\u2019t know, comic book-y. Maybe that\u2019s just the meme of it rubbing off unfavorably though, YMMV. Also while NYC has some neat ideas and characters in it, the overall setting never really clicked for me. The whole Midnight Siege for NYC metaplot thing is a cool and all but I honestly think that NYC before the Camarilla takeover would have been a more interesting setting: the Camarilla stronghold on Manhattan Island, the quarreling Sabbat bishoprics in the Outer Bureaus, the Anarch &amp; Independent enclaves strewn throughout - I think it would have had more sauce, but maybe that\u2019s just me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T14:01:34-08:00","id":1555766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555433#post1555433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago and Constantnople by Night were my favorite city books with the Fall of London &amp; Berlin by Night as my least favorite.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you Lysander about both Constantinople and Chicago, but I also liked Fall of London too. It really made you feel like you were in a British city (maybe because Modiphius is a British company).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-22T15:03:01-08:00","id":1555770,"title":"","content":"Montreal and Constantinople are by far my favorite.<br /> <br /> Least... I never enjoyed New York, that only changed after playing Coteries and Shadows (specially this one).<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T02:38:55-08:00","id":1555789,"title":"","content":"I really likes constantinople and mexico city by night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Fall of london was genuinly bad, but im not sure it counts. Even los angeles had Bela lugosi so theirs positives even their.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 11-23-2025, 08:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T16:53:27-08:00","id":1555814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555765#post1555765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chicago of course is the gold standard really. While I\u2019m someone who isn\u2019t a huge fan of all the 2nd edition killings, both are still all-timers in my opinion</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it has two problems, one compounding the other.<br /> <br /> First, why did it had <b><i>both</i></b> a Prince and a Primigen? Domains aren't modern states with a president and a senate, those institutions are meant to be interchangeable, not simultaneous.<br /> <br /> Second, it was taken even by the devs as gospel for how Camarilla cities structure themselves. The problem isn't the city's structure itself, but how much it solidified as the to-go way for making a Domain. Even today we have lots of STs that struggle with their settings because they feel obliged to make every city have the same institutions and stuff as Chicago, even when they're very different places.<br /> <br /> The core book painted a picture where cities vary a lot, and many configurations can exist within the Camarilla, but Chicago became the only right way to do so.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodline</i>'s Santa Monica is a far more interesting starting point to describe a &quot;standard&quot; Camarilla Domain in my opinion than Chicago, because it actually works as a bare-bones structure you can build upon instead of a massive system you have to figure out how to disassemble.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555765#post1555765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">outside of the secret Lasombra</div> </div> </div> </div>My major gripe with D.C. is that it was a missed opportunity to showcase how you shouldn't be too attached to expectations. Vitel's shouldn't have been a secret at all. Why?<br /> <br /> Sure it plays to the stereotypes about clan affiliations, but it also plays those stereotypes as absolutes while ignores the actual information in the books.<br /> <br /> There's no rule against a Lasombra becoming Prince. There's no rule about any clan or bloodline assuming any role within the Camarilla, except as a Justicar (and even then this isn't an unbreakable rule). Members of every clan can diverge. And the Prince is simply the strongest monster around that wants the title. Why should Vitel have to hide his clan at all? I'm talking it from the conceptual level, not his background as it came to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555765#post1555765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus the timeline gives me a headache when I try to square it with Demon, KotE, &amp; Bloodlines (which tbh I largely ignore in practice). Still some great work has been done on these very forums to flesh out the setting and that deserves a mention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also Mage, LA is important to Mage. It's possibly the single most used city for metaplot events and headquarters for shenanigans in the game. If you run every line as canon in your game there's no way to not have a crossover in LA.<br /> <br /> I think the problem with LA was mostly a problem with the devs not having really thought well what a rebellion could look like after success. LA is just the absence of a Prince, anarchy less as a system or policy and simply as the state of lawlessness and how it was perceived in the 90s in big cities within stable countries. It was a big &quot;so what, now?&quot;<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555765#post1555765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the Tzimisce Antedeluviam being under NYC thing, while pretty funny and cool in theory, does more harm than good to the setting in theory long run.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was another spin on a problem the setting had with many other things, especially Noddism: legends were established, but then deepening them seemed easier than making conflicting alternatives that could shake things up, sow doubt and give STs options.<br /> <br /> Strictly speaking that thing isn't anything in particular, it <i>may be</i>. It may be almost anything you can think. [Tzimisce] is simply the easiest conclusion for people used to Vicissitude's flesh-crafting. Even in the book <i>Gehenna</i> only one scenario assumes the NYC's Big Bad Blob to be something relevant, and that book is adamant in saying it isn't canon and I take that to heart. But in the end they never managed to write about it without focusing on this specific legend, and that's an error.<br /> <br /> VtR in this sense goes to great lengths to make sure you have conflicting narratives, which not only deepens the sense of unknown and mystery, but also feeds the ST with ideas to use, discard and tweak, and less pressure to make any particular version the real one.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555765#post1555765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole Midnight Siege for NYC metaplot thing is a cool and all but I honestly think that NYC before the Camarilla takeover would have been a more interesting setting: the Camarilla stronghold on Manhattan Island, the quarreling Sabbat bishoprics in the Outer Bureaus, the Anarch &amp; Independent enclaves strewn throughout - I think it would have had more sauce, but maybe that\u2019s just me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't just you, I think so, too. A dynamic setting where various factions fight (and make truces) is far more compelling than just a recent recovery, even because that would make easier for STs to put the city in whatever hands they want just by deciding the conflict resolved how they want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T17:24:48-08:00","id":1555816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555814#post1555814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it has two problems, one compounding the other.<br /> <br /> First, why did it had <b><i>both</i></b> a Prince and a Primigen? Domains aren't modern states with a president and a senate, those institutions are meant to be interchangeable, not simultaneous.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm confused by this idea because if a city has enough vampires to have a prince they will absolutely have enough vampires to have a Primogen. The Primogen is everyone who either doesn't want to be Prince but is powerful enough to dictate policy in the city.<br /> <br /> It's like when Beckett's Jyhad Diary said Chicago didn't need a Prince because it had a Primogen, I was like, &quot;So, Critias is the Prince.&quot;<br /> <br /> Because if there's a Primogen, there is whoever is the most powerful Primogen and he's the Prince. Saying otherwise is silly. Vampires are hierarchical creatures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Second, it was taken even by the devs as gospel for how Camarilla cities structure themselves. The problem isn't the city's structure itself, but how much it solidified as the to-go way for making a Domain. Even today we have lots of STs that struggle with their settings because they feel obliged to make every city have the same institutions and stuff as Chicago, even when they're very different places. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I think the irony is that no one can really think of a better way to run V:TM games that creates drama. We've had many other non-Prince/Primogen/Elders/Anarchs settings but they really don't generate the kind of intrigue that players love. It's even infected the Anarchs and why they have Barons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Bloodline</i>'s Santa Monica is a far more interesting starting point to describe a &quot;standard&quot; Camarilla Domain in my opinion than Chicago, because it actually works as a bare-bones structure you can build upon instead of a massive system you have to figure out how to disassemble. </div> </div> </div>Is it? Because I thought it was Therese's Barony and everyone answered to her. There's just not enough vampires to be a Primogen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My major gripe with D.C. is that it was a missed opportunity to showcase how you shouldn't be too attached to expectations. Vitel's shouldn't have been a secret at all. Why?<br /> <br /> Sure it plays to the stereotypes about clan affiliations, but it also plays those stereotypes as absolutes while ignores the actual information in the books.<br /> <br /> There's no rule against a Lasombra becoming Prince. There's no rule about any clan or bloodline assuming any role within the Camarilla, except as a Justicar (and even then this isn't an unbreakable rule). Members of every clan can diverge. And the Prince is simply the strongest monster around that wants the title. Why should Vitel have to hide his clan at all? I'm talking it from the conceptual level, not his background as it came to be. </div> </div> </div>I thought it wasn't because Vitel was a Lasombra but the fact he was someone that was nearly universally reviled by both the Sabbat and Camarilla both in his true identity. Mind you, he did murder the previous Prince but I am like Flemeth in Dragon Age that, &quot;Yeah, kings do that all the time. It's how they become kings.&quot;<br /> <br /> FYI - I tried to bring Monica Black into the 5th Edition Era but she got rejected and another Sejanus childe was created instead for Children of the Blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also Mage, LA is important to Mage. It's possibly the single most used city for metaplot events and headquarters for shenanigans in the game. If you run every line as canon in your game there's no way to not have a crossover in LA.<br /> <br /> I think the problem with LA was mostly a problem with the devs not having really thought well what a rebellion could look like after success. LA is just the absence of a Prince, anarchy less as a system or policy and simply as the state of lawlessness and how it was perceived in the 90s in big cities within stable countries. It was a big &quot;so what, now?&quot; </div> </div> </div>As you mentioned above, the Chicago system is so inherent to vampire even the Anarchs copied it with Barons initially supposed to be &quot;ironic&quot; but getting actually accepted as the defacto system for Anarchs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Strictly speaking that thing isn't anything in particular, it <i>may be</i>. It may be almost anything you can think. [Tzimisce] is simply the easiest conclusion for people used to Vicissitude's flesh-crafting. Even in the book <i>Gehenna</i> only one scenario assumes the NYC's Big Bad Blob to be something relevant, and that book is adamant in saying it isn't canon and I take that to heart. But in the end they never managed to write about it without focusing on this specific legend, and that's an error. </div> </div> </div>In Gehenna, the PCs slay the giant flesh monster and permanently break the masquerade. It was like, &quot;There's no real other way to make this thing relevant, so why not do something immensely stupid?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> VtR in this sense goes to great lengths to make sure you have conflicting narratives, which not only deepens the sense of unknown and mystery, but also feeds the ST with ideas to use, discard and tweak, and less pressure to make any particular version the real one. </div> </div> </div>I have my issues as I love Noddism but Requiem does have a good sense of mystery. Sadly, the attempt to give Chronicles' sense of mystery to Werewolf was a massive misfire.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oral history doesn't really tell us what happened way back when.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dude, oral history has unchanging stories 12,000 years later.&quot;<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It isn't just you, I think so, too. A dynamic setting where various factions fight (and make truces) is far more compelling than just a recent recovery, even because that would make easier for STs to put the city in whatever hands they want just by deciding the conflict resolved how they want. </div> </div> </div>I like what they did with New York by Night but that's because they more or less got out of the transition period depicted in the books. However, I don't think the Kindred wars as depicted in so many places are that interesting a concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-23T21:44:19-08:00","id":1555820,"title":"","content":"As a native New Englander, I found Dark Colony's Triad and Redcoats terribly silly. New York By Night was an improvement, even if setting it after the end of the war instead of making the war the focus of a chronicle was a missed opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-24T21:46:43-08:00","id":1555837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm confused by this idea because if a city has enough vampires to have a prince they will absolutely have enough vampires to have a Primogen. The Primogen is everyone who either doesn't want to be Prince but is powerful enough to dictate policy in the city.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have the same role. It's literally like having both a President and a King with the same powers.<br /> <br /> It has nothing to do with the size of the city, it has to do with someone being powerful enough to claim Domain or having to share power with others.<br /> <br /> Even if each Primogen only cares for their clan, it's still a heavy interference in the power of the Prince if the city has one. No autocrat would accept such interference, such parallel power. If they have no choice, then it's the Primogen that don't need a Prince to interfere in their affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are hierarchical creatures.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they're not, that's the big problem with Chicago.<br /> <br /> It created a notion of how vampires structure formal power that isn't really a thing in their nature nor was meant to be a thing in the setting outside specific situations.<br /> <br /> Vampires are egotistical and greedy. Creating titles and whatnot isn't a matter of hierarchy, but of appeasing their vanity. Even then most don't care that much and are happy with feeding grounds and access to the powers that be. What titles actually exist are well beneath those who really have power, because those just take what they want.<br /> <br /> Most of the hierarchy in Chicago, that is copied elsewhere, is interesting for players not because they say something about Vampires, but because they make the setting easier to digest when we have such a lack of other examples of how they could organize.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think the irony is that no one can really think of a better way to run V:TM games that creates drama. We've had many other non-Prince/Primogen/Elders/Anarchs settings but they really don't generate the kind of intrigue that players love. It's even infected the Anarchs and why they have Barons.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you understood what I said, because I never said a city could have nothing at all to vie for.<br /> <br /> What I said was that DeLacroix's LA, as far as the Camarilla part goes, worked as the basic arrangement. It has only the Prince and Sheriff as formal roles, and it doesn't really need more. There are other powerful kindred he has to negotiate with, even something that resembles a Primogen, but no formal titles are needed, and there's the very point I'm making that they were as much potential allies as enemies to DeLacroix because he was a particularly weak Prince, although even then he wasn't someone they were willing to just ignore, he was still personally dangerous.<br /> <br /> From there you can build a lot of other things. You may have minimalist structures for small Domains (or like LA, ones with a small Camarilla presence). You may have whichever titles you need in your city and ignore the rest. You can have other vampires that can stand to the Prince in some way assume their own self-made titles (which is mostly what the Barons are). You may have a Primogen-that-isn't, a group that exists as a challenge to the power of the Prince, not as a part of the same structure.<br /> <br /> You can have lots of things, even Chicago. You just don't have to be another Chicago. And Chicago didn't need a Prince at all.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? Because I thought it was Therese's Barony and everyone answered to her. There's just not enough vampires to be a Primogen.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's besides the point, even because in this sense it was disputed territory.<br /> <br /> DeLacroix claimed the entirety of LA as Domain, and as powerful as the Barons were, none of them directly disputed this to his face.<br /> <br /> His actual power varied as the Barons and other relevant Kindred opposed him more or less, and Therese was more his ally than of any other Baron, so they kind of shared Santa Monica.<br /> <br /> So much so that the Fledgling remained there, and while you get to do a lot of things for a lot of people in the game, you're above all else DeLacroix's thug until further notice.<br /> <br /> My point isn't if the city had size for one thing or the other, but that its Camarilla part worked with just two titles.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it wasn't because Vitel was a Lasombra but the fact he was someone that was nearly universally reviled by both the Sabbat and Camarilla both in his true identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the Watsonian perspective, you have to keep in mind that he wasn't a secret Lasombra because he was reviled, he was made reviled because the devs wanted him to be a secret Lasombra.<br /> <br /> And the whole &quot;secret identity&quot; shenanigan didn't really depend on him taking on the role of a Ventrue. He could have pretended to be a Lasombra <i>Antitribu</i> all along.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As you mentioned above, the Chicago system is so inherent to vampire even the Anarchs copied it with Barons initially supposed to be &quot;ironic&quot; but getting actually accepted as the defacto system for Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which doesn't change what I said about them not knowing what to do with an Anarch Domain.<br /> <br /> Even then the Barons aren't so much Princes as they are gang bosses.<br /> <br /> They control small-ish territories and have to go to turf wars if they want something more, or to negotiate if they want access to resources and areas without such wars.<br /> <br /> None of them has the power or cohesion needed to actually manage the city as a whole, which is what a Prince or a Primogen does.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Gehenna, the PCs slay the giant flesh monster and permanently break the masquerade. It was like, &quot;There's no real other way to make this thing relevant, so why not do something immensely stupid?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the price of never exploring any possibility besides the same legend again and again. When push comes to shove you don't have much else to do, any creative use would need a build up you don't have the time for anymore.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have my issues as I love Noddism but Requiem does have a good sense of mystery. Sadly, the attempt to give Chronicles' sense of mystery to Werewolf was a massive misfire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Noddism isn't the problem, it has never been.<br /> <br /> It was not exploring anything else because Noddism was the low hanging fruit that was the problem.<br /> <br /> Through the whole of the three original editions WoD had this problem where once a myth is given the devs will explore it as much as possible because it was easy drama.<br /> <br /> While this gave players a sense of deepening and coveted answers, it also stripped things of mystery and made it hard to convince that other legends could be just as valid. Which was a problem every single time they tried, when they finally noticed they needed other legends to tell some stories.<br /> <br /> Requiem 2nd Edition gives you 4 or 5 legends from the get go with each clan, and a bunch more in other places. The book about VII solves the problem of exploring them without answering the mystery by being four contradictory books in one, four complete and meaningful answers to whatever the group is, so the ST has the inspiration and the tools to easily build their own version.<br /> <br /> And as I said, myths are more important because of what they inspire people to do than because of any reality behind them. If all the energy spent deepening Noddism had been spent in making factions based on interpretations of it and other things, and their influence and activities, we could have plenty of Noddism and other things without ever having to get actual evidence for anything.<br /> <br /> But W5 isn't that, either, it is... I think it is just stupidity.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555816#post1555816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like what they did with New York by Night but that's because they more or less got out of the transition period depicted in the books. However, I don't think the Kindred wars as depicted in so many places are that interesting a concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is, at least for this one city. It didn't have to be an actual war, but a city divided between factions trying to coexist without mutual annihilation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T05:35:03-08:00","id":1555843,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not sure if this is the most apt place to put this, but one of the MASQUERADE cities I think about most is Victorian London during the period when Valerius was obviously working towards a transformation from Regent into a Camarilla Prince (Between the late 1840s and the early 1880s), with something of a \u2018Gold Rush\u2019 as newcomers attempt to stake their claims in what was arguably the single most powerful &amp; important metropolis on Earth, presumably whilst old hands manoeuvre for or against the transition from Regency to Princedom, as well as the new openness.<br /> <br /> All whilst Mithras remains the proverbial Elephant In The Room without actually leaving anything but his long, ice cold shadow over London during the course of a lengthy absence: there\u2019s no guarantee that he\u2019ll come back, but if he does return and doesn\u2019t approve of goings on, well \u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> I\u2019m also curious about Rome as a Kindred city: my impression is that it was a place to visit rather than a place to put down roots for much of the Christian era (Being something of a minefield of supernatural relics &amp; oddities even without considering the World Religion in prolonged residence) and very clearly a city that the vampires have no exclusive title to.<br /> <br /> On the other hand it\u2019s too juicy a major city (and has too many layers of history to mine), with significant ties to more than one Clan, so it\u2019s impossible to imagine there not being a steadily growing Vampire presence in such a population centre - especially after government of the city was taken into purely secular hands - however precarious it\u2019s position.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T05:35:42-08:00","id":1555844,"title":"","content":"Almost forgot to add: also \u2018ROMA SUB ROSA\u2019 would be an excellent title for a VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE sourcebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-25T10:24:20-08:00","id":1555857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1555342-your-favorite-and-least-favorite-v-tm-cities?p=1555844#post1555844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost forgot to add: also \u2018ROMA SUB ROSA\u2019 would be an excellent title for a VAMPIRE: THE MASQUERADE sourcebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've had that thought for years after I learned the symbolic meaning of roses for Romans! Perfect for the Masquerade and its classic rose covers. I think I first became aware of it in Steven Saylor's books on Gordianus the Finder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-11-27T13:49:07-08:00","id":1555919,"title":"","content":"Ditto! Though in my case it may have been one of his other Roman novels that introduced me to Mr Saylor\u2019s work and the supremely World of Darkness-appropriate title of his main series.<br /> <br /> Though even with that in mind, it amuses me to imagine that a key reason Darius the Nosferatu, Chief Tour Guide and reluctant sometime Prince of Roma, has survived to see the Modern Nights is that while he\u2019s an Ancient, he\u2019s not an Ancient <i>Roman*</i> - he\u2019s never been in a position to act like he runs the place, being a foreigner to start with and obliged to spend eternity as a Nosferatu to boot.<br /> <br /> The other is that \u2018Chief Tour Guide\u2019 is his preferred title - even in Vampire society people usually pay tour guides without planning to kill them so they can run their very own tours.<br /> <br /> <br /> *It also amuses me to imagine that Darius is almost the only veteran of Ancient Rome to speak with an accent modern Italians would recognise as Pure Roma - the others have never deigned to lose their \u2018Veni, Vidi, Vici\u2019, but a Nosferatu needs all the help they can get to ensure listeners stick around long enough to hold a civil conversation.<br /> <br /> How he managers to sound like a man with a five-pack-a-day smoking habit despite having died long before tobacco ever left the Americas remains a question for the ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}